    "action": "correct",
    "reason": "The PR [ev-5dfd16d143dd] fixes two cases: an optional `ssh`/`altssh` subdomain in repo URLs (#19314, [ev-232d1413254c]) and a username in `https?` repo URLs (#15700, Azure DevOps, [ev-636f706e3247]). It changes both util/webhook and applicationset/webhook [ev-f1f886c7e03b]. The proposed condition covers only the ssh/altssh case, so it misses exposed environments that use https://user@host URLs. It is also fully undecidable even though the repo URLs are readable from Application/ApplicationSet repoURL fields. Only the external part, whether the git provider actually sends webhooks to Argo CD, belongs in an undecidable leaf.",
